  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at The Magic Stick in Detroit, Michigan, on Monday, October 4, 2004 [1]. This audience recording, captured in 320kbps MP3 format, runs for 63 minutes and includes all 18 songs from the setlist [1]. The show is the 60th in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous recording from May 2004 [3]. The setlist features a mix of familiar tracks and rare appearances, including “International Small Arms Traffic Blues” and “First Few Desperate Hours” [1]. Notably, the recording contains the first archived performance of “Dilaudid” and “This Year,” as well as the only archived performance of “Rockin' Rockin' Pet Store” [1]. The show also includes “Short Song About the 10 Freeway,” which is considered rare with only five archived performances, and “Orange,” a Furniture Huschle cover, which is mythically rare with just two archived performances [1]. The set concludes with an encore featuring “Raja Vocative,” a bustout that had not appeared in 35 previous archived shows, and “No Children” [1]. One listener, writing in 2024 about this specific recording, shared that hearing “This Year” played live for one of the first times made them unexpectedly emotional [2]. The recording is highly rated, holding a 5/5 average from one listener [1].",
